# Content tabs

Use [Material content tabs](https://squidfunk.github.io/mkdocs-material/reference/content-tabs/) for two or more alternative views of the same thing, such as a shorthand YAML form and the full form. `pymdownx.tabbed` and `pymdownx.superfences` are enabled, and `content.tabs.link` keeps every tab with the same label in sync. Do not use a tab for the next step in a sequence.

A tab starts with `=== "Label"`. Indent its body by four spaces.

````markdown
=== "Shorthand"

    ```yaml
    - image: assets/logo.png
    ```

=== "Full form"

    ```yaml
    - image:
        source: assets/logo.png
    ```
````

- Use the same label for the same alternative on every page. Clicking "Shorthand" selects every "Shorthand" tab.
- A tab that holds one code block has no extra horizontal padding. A tab with several blocks does.
- Nest tabs in an admonition by indenting the `===` lines another four spaces under the admonition body.
- An anchor is added to each tab. The slug is the label in lower case.
- A tab can contain another tab group. Indent the inner `===` lines another four spaces. One level is enough for these pages.
